{
  "title": "不替眾神織衣",
  "title_en": "Not Weaving for the Gods",
  "series": "神話未完成",
  "series_en": "Myths in the Making",
  "volume": 12,
  "model": "史旺姬",
  "creator": "史旺基 Swanky",
  "slug": "swanky-ji-not-weaving-for-gods",
  "date": "2026-10-21",
  "count": 36,
  "cover_photo": 24,
  "setting": "染坊與織機之間的山城",
  "subtitle": "把被看不見的人，織進會被看見的地方。",
  "subtitle_en": "Weaving unseen lives into a place where they can be seen.",
  "lead": "秤盤決定羊毛的重量，神殿決定布上的故事。織工每天走過染坊、紡紗廊與山坡，逐漸發現：那些讓布成形的人，始終不在圖案裡。她開始換一種織法。",
  "lead_en": "The scales determine the weight of wool; the temple determines the stories on the cloth. Walking between the dye house, the spinning gallery and the hillside, a weaver notices that the people who make the cloth are absent from its images. She begins to weave differently.",
  "statement": "秤盤決定羊毛的重量，神殿決定布上的故事。織工每天走過染坊、紡紗廊與山坡，逐漸發現：那些讓布成形的人，始終不在圖案裡。她開始換一種織法。\n\n布被撕開以後，她沒有把它藏起來。她把破口連同人的工作一起掛在市集，讓每一雙眼睛重新讀它。最後留下的紅線很細，只夠表明：下一塊布，由她決定從哪裡開始。",
  "statement_en": "The scales determine the weight of wool; the temple determines the stories on the cloth. Walking between the dye house, the spinning gallery and the hillside, a weaver notices that the people who make the cloth are absent from its images. She begins to weave differently.\n\nWhen the cloth is torn, she does not hide it. She hangs its wounds and its working lives in the market, where every pair of eyes can read it anew. The red thread she leaves is slender: just enough to mark that the next cloth will begin where she chooses.",
  "afterword": "布被撕開以後，她沒有把它藏起來。她把破口連同人的工作一起掛在市集，讓每一雙眼睛重新讀它。最後留下的紅線很細，只夠表明：下一塊布，由她決定從哪裡開始。",
  "afterword_en": "When the cloth is torn, she does not hide it. She hangs its wounds and its working lives in the market, where every pair of eyes can read it anew. The red thread she leaves is slender: just enough to mark that the next cloth will begin where she chooses.",
  "series_statement": "《神話未完成》\n史旺姬走進流傳至今的神話，留下它最核心的問題，讓它面對今天的生活。神話一直被講述、被使用，所以還沒有完成。",
  "series_statement_en": "Myths in the Making\nSwanky Ji steps into myths that are still being told, keeps the question at their heart, and lets it meet the life we live now. A myth that is still told and still used is not yet finished.",
  "story_zh": "本冊取材自 Ovid《變形記》卷六的 Arachne 故事；詩中女神稱 Pallas，即雅典娜。原典中的織物揭示眾神的欺騙，本冊則把地方與勞動者放在中央。神殿委託、小城與市集懸布的結局是原創改寫。她不變成蜘蛛，而以亞麻開始新作；這個結尾也回應 Pliny《博物志》7.196 將 Arachne 記為亞麻與網之發明者的古代傳統。服裝、空間與工藝場景為創作組合。",
  "story_en": "This book draws on the story of Arachne in Book VI of Ovid’s Metamorphoses. The goddess is called Pallas, or Athena. Where the original cloth exposes divine deception, this retelling places landscapes and working people at its centre. The temple commission, the town and the ending in the market are original inventions. Arachne does not become a spider; she begins another work in flax. This ending also responds to the ancient tradition in Pliny’s Natural History 7.196 that credits Arachne with the invention of flax-working and nets. Clothing, spaces and scenes of craft are creative composites.",
  "sources_zh": "故事參考：Ovid · Metamorphoses VI (Latin)（https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=Perseus:text:1999.02.0029:book=6:card=1）；Pliny · Naturalis Historia VII (Latin)（https://penelope.uchicago.edu/Thayer/L/Roman/Texts/Pliny_the_Elder/7*.html）",
  "sources_en": "Story references: Ovid · Metamorphoses VI (Latin) (https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=Perseus:text:1999.02.0029:book=6:card=1); Pliny · Naturalis Historia VII (Latin) (https://penelope.uchicago.edu/Thayer/L/Roman/Texts/Pliny_the_Elder/7*.html)",
  "credit": "史旺姬 × 史旺基｜神話未完成・第十二冊",
  "credit_en": "Swanky Ji × Swanky | Myths in the Making · Volume Twelve",
